<div class="w3-container">
  <p>
    Before an issuer can sign credentials with an X.509 certificate, its signing
    key needs a certificate from a CA. Run the steps below in order. The private
    key is created in the issuer's wallet and never leaves it: the CA only sees a
    certificate signing request (CSR).
  </p>
  <p>
    When onboarding is complete, issue a credential with
    <b>Issue Credential &rarr; SD-JWT VC (X.509 certificate)</b>. The credential
    carries the certificate chain in its <code>x5c</code> header in place of a DID
    <code>kid</code>.
  </p>
</div>
